{# Charmed Apache Spark release notes template.

   Modelled on the published Charmed Apache Spark release notes in
   canonical/spark-k8s-bundle (docs/reference/releases/revision-*.md on the
   track/* branches), e.g.
   https://canonical.com/data/spark/docs/3.5/reference/releases/revision-6/

   Differences from base.md.j2 (all deliberate, to match the published docs):
     * MyST frontmatter with an html_meta description and a MyST anchor.
     * Title is "Charmed Apache Spark (revision N)"; the date is a plain line
       (e.g. "July 29th, 2026"), not bold.
     * Links line is "Charmhub: <channel> | Docs | Deploy guide |
       System requirements".
     * Section names/order follow the Spark docs, NOT the DA186 default order:
       Features, Enhancements, Bug Fixes, Breaking Changes,
       Documentation improvements, Security, Compatibility, Acknowledgements.
       ("Enhancements" is Spark's name for DA186's "Other improvements";
       "Documentation improvements" is a Spark-specific extra section.)
     * Within each section, entries are grouped under per-component `###`
       subheadings (Apache Kyuubi, Apache Spark History Server, Spark
       Integration Hub, Apache Spark Client snap, Canonical security
       maintained OCI Images for Apache Spark, Charmed Apache Spark Terraform
       Module, spark8t) — the builder cannot infer components, so it emits a
       flat list per section and the agent regroups it.
     * Security is a CVE table (reStructuredText grid table in an eval-rst
       block), not a changelog category.
     * Compatibility is a reStructuredText grid table in an eval-rst block
       with the columns: Component | Hardware architecture | Channel |
       Artifact | Revision | Minimum Juju version | Recommended Juju version.

   Product-wide scope: Charmed Apache Spark release notes cover the whole
   solution, not just one repository — the charms (kyuubi-k8s,
   spark-history-server-k8s, spark-integration-hub-k8s), the OCI images
   (charmed-spark-rock, spark-integration-hub-rock), the spark-client snap,
   the spark8t library and the Terraform module (spark-k8s-bundle).
   Never title a Charmed Apache Spark release notes document after a single
   component such as the Terraform module.
#}
